  {
   "id": 639906,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/dff22ab373273b12.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Abby Augarten/Ag Water Exchange)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the productivity of corn fields based on their nitrogen supply.</p>\n<p>Make a claim based on this graph.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1247143,
     "content_html": "Fields with more than one source of nitrogen tend to be more productive."
    },
    {
     "id": 1247142,
     "content_html": "The most popular nitrogen source is planting legumes."
    },
    {
     "id": 1247141,
     "content_html": "Fields with artificial nitrogen fertilizer tend to be more productive."
    },
    {
     "id": 1247140,
     "content_html": "Almost all fields use manure as a partial source of nitrogen."
    }
   ],
